invariant: INV-25
file: srv_parser_ext.c
catches: srv_test
reason: read_supported_versions stops holding versions<2..254> to an even
  byte count, so a list whose last version is one byte short is read as a
  whole one: rb_u16 supplies a zero for the byte that is not there, and two
  encodings name one version list. RFC 9846 §4.2.1 makes every entry two
  bytes. test/srv_parser_tests.h sends an odd list whose versions fill the
  extension, which the exact-fill check cannot refuse first.

--- old
    if (e->err || list_len < 2 || (list_len & 1) != 0 || list_len > rb_left(e)) {
--- new
    if (e->err || list_len < 2 || list_len > rb_left(e)) {
